{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "def sort_matrix(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a matrix by the sum of its rows in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    \n    def _calculate_row_sum(row: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements in a single row.\"\"\"\n        return sum(row)\n\n    # Pair each row with its sum\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        rows_with_sums.append((_calculate_row_sum(row), row))\n\n    # Sort these pairs based on the row sums\n    rows_with_sums.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    # Extract the sorted rows to form the new matrix\n    sorted_matrix = [row for sum_val, row in rows_with_sums]\n\n    return sorted_matrix"}
