{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\"\"\"\n\n    class NewmanConwaySequence:\n        \"\"\"Encapsulates the logic and state (memoization cache) for calculating Newman-Conway sequence numbers.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self):\n            # Initializes the cache with the base cases P(1)=1 and P(2)=1.\n            self._cache = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n        def compute(self, k: int) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Recursively computes P(k) with memoization for k > 0.\"\"\"\n            if k in self._cache:\n                return self._cache[k]\n            \n            # P(k) = P(P(k - 1)) + P(k - P(k - 1)) for k > 2\n            p_k_minus_1 = self.compute(k - 1)\n            result = self.compute(p_k_minus_1) + self.compute(k - p_k_minus_1)\n            self._cache[k] = result\n            return result\n\n    # Uses a function attribute to store a single instance of NewmanConwaySequence.\n    # This ensures the cache is persistent across multiple calls to 'sequence(n)'.\n    if not hasattr(sequence, '_calculator'):\n        sequence._calculator = NewmanConwaySequence()\n\n    return sequence._calculator.compute(n)"}
