{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "def next_smallest_palindrome(n: int) -> int:\n    def _is_palindrome(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is a palindrome.\"\"\"\n        s = str(num)\n        return s == s[::-1]\n\n    def _build_palindrome(half_str: str, is_odd_length: bool) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Constructs an integer palindrome from its string representation of the first half.\"\"\"\n        first_part = half_str\n        if is_odd_length:\n            # If the palindrome has an odd number of digits, half_str includes the middle digit.\n            # The second part is the reverse of the first part excluding the middle digit.\n            second_part = half_str[:-1][::-1]\n        else:\n            # If the palindrome has an even number of digits, half_str is exactly half the digits.\n            # The second part is the reverse of the entire first half.\n            second_part = half_str[::-1]\n        return int(first_part + second_part)\n\n    def _increment_half(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Increments the numeric value represented by the string s, handling carry-overs.\"\"\"\n        num = int(s) + 1\n        return str(num)\n\n    # Special handling for single-digit numbers. For n <= 9, the next smallest palindrome is 11.\n    # The requirement is that it must be strictly greater than n.\n    if n < 10:\n        return 11\n\n    s = str(n)\n    length = len(s)\n    is_odd_length = (length % 2 == 1)\n\n    # first_half_len is the length of the string segment that forms the first half,\n    # including the middle digit if the total length is odd.\n    first_half_len = (length + 1) // 2\n    first_half_str = s[:first_half_len]\n\n    # Attempt to build a palindrome using the current first half of 'n'.\n    candidate_palindrome = _build_palindrome(first_half_str, is_odd_length)\n\n    # If this candidate palindrome is already strictly greater than n, it is the answer.\n    if candidate_palindrome > n:\n        return candidate_palindrome\n    else:\n        # If not, increment the first half and build a new palindrome.\n        first_half_str_inc = _increment_half(first_half_str)\n\n        # Determine the parity for the new palindrome. If incrementing the half\n        # increased its length (e.g., \"9\" -> \"10\"), the new palindrome will typically\n        # have an odd number of digits and be one digit longer than the original.\n        current_is_odd_length = is_odd_length\n        if len(first_half_str_inc) > first_half_len:\n            current_is_odd_length = True # This covers cases like 99 -> 101, 999 -> 10001\n\n        new_palindrome = _build_palindrome(first_half_str_inc, current_is_odd_length)\n        return new_palindrome"}
