{"task_id": "Mbpp/128", "solution": "def long_words(n: int, text_content: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies words from a given string that have a length strictly greater than n.\n    Returns a list of qualifying words.\n    \"\"\"\n    words = text_content.split(' ')\n    result = []\n    for word in words:\n        if len(word) > n:\n            result.append(word)\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "def max_occurrences(items: list) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the item with the maximum frequency in a given list.\n\n    Args:\n        items: A list of comparable items.\n\n    Returns:\n        The item with the highest frequency. If the list is empty,\n        returns None. If multiple items share the maximum frequency,\n        any one of them is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items:\n        return None\n\n    # Use a dictionary to store frequencies\n    frequency_map = {}\n    for item in items:\n        frequency_map[item] = frequency_map.get(item, 0) + 1\n\n    # Find the item with the maximum frequency\n    max_item = None\n    max_freq = -1\n    for item, freq in frequency_map.items():\n        if freq > max_freq:\n            max_freq = freq\n            max_item = item\n    return max_item"}
