{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "def reverse_vowels(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Reverses only the vowels in a given string, where 'y' is not a vowel.\n    \n    This function identifies vowels (a, e, i, o, u, case-insensitive), stores them,\n    and then replaces them in reverse order in their original positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a character is a vowel (a, e, i, o, u, case-insensitive, excluding y/Y).\"\"\"\n        return char.lower() in 'aeiou'\n\n    char_list = list(s)\n    vowel_indices = []\n    vowels_found = []\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(char_list):\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            vowel_indices.append(i)\n            vowels_found.append(char)\n\n    vowels_found.reverse()\n\n    for i, vowel_index in enumerate(vowel_indices):\n        char_list[vowel_index] = vowels_found[i]\n\n    return \"\".join(char_list)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def sum(num1, num2):\n    def _get_divisors(number: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates all positive divisors of a given integer.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return []\n        number = abs(number)\n        divs = []\n        for i in range(1, int(number**0.5) + 1):\n            if number % i == 0:\n                divs.append(i)\n                if i * i != number:\n                    divs.append(number // i)\n        return sorted(divs)\n\n    def get_common_divisors_internal(n1: int, n2: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Computes the positive common divisors of two integers.\"\"\"\n        divisors1 = set(_get_divisors(n1))\n        divisors2 = set(_get_divisors(n2))\n        return sorted(list(divisors1.intersection(divisors2)))\n\n    common_divs = get_common_divisors_internal(num1, num2)\n    return sum(common_divs)"}
