{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "def larg_nnum(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes a list and an integer n and returns a list containing the n largest items from the list.\n    If n is non-positive, an empty list is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    if len(input_list) <= n:\n        return sorted(input_list, reverse=True)\n\n    sorted_list = sorted(input_list, reverse=True)\n    return sorted_list[:n]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def _canonicalize_tuple(tup: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Converts a tuple into its canonical form by sorting its elements.\"\"\"\n    return tuple(sorted(tup))\ndef check_occurences(input_list: list[tuple]) -> dict[tuple, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the occurrences of unique canonicalized tuples within a list.\n    It returns a dictionary mapping canonicalized tuples to their counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for tup in input_list:\n        canonical_tup = _canonicalize_tuple(tup)\n        counts[canonical_tup] = counts.get(canonical_tup, 0) + 1\n    return counts"}
