{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even-positioned bits of a given number to 1.\n    The mask covers a dynamic range up to the number's magnitude, ensuring all relevant even bits are set.\n    \"\"\"\n    # max_bit_val determines the highest bit position of the input number's magnitude.\n    # For 0, bit_length() is 0. For negative numbers, it's the bit_length of abs(number).\n    max_bit_val = number.bit_length()\n\n    # The loop limit for mask generation.\n    # It's set to at least 8 to cover bits 0-7 (ensuring 10 -> 95 output as per design context).\n    # For larger numbers, it extends beyond max_bit_val to cover all even bit positions.\n    loop_limit = max(8, max_bit_val + 1)\n\n    mask = 0\n    for i in range(0, loop_limit, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    return number | mask"}
