{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence for the given string.\n\n    Args:\n        s: The input string.\n\n    Returns:\n        The length of the longest palindromic subsequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the LPS for substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Every single character is a palindrome of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the dp table by increasing substring length\n    for L in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - L + 1):\n            j = i + L - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j] and L == 2:\n                dp[i][j] = 2\n            elif s[i] == s[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i+1][j-1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i][j-1], dp[i+1][j])\n\n    return dp[0][n-1]"}
