{"task_id": "Mbpp/273", "solution": "def substract_elements(tuple1: tuple[int, ...], tuple2: tuple[int, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Subtracts elements of the second tuple from corresponding elements of the first tuple.\n    Assumes inputs are two tuples of equal length containing numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    result_list = [t1 - t2 for t1, t2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2)]\n    return tuple(result_list)"}
