{"task_id": "Mbpp/566", "solution": "class NonNegativeInteger:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates a non-negative integer and provides digit sum calculation.\n    It validates that the input value is a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        if not isinstance(value, int) or value < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer\")\n        self._value = value\n\n    def calculate_sum_of_digits(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates and returns the sum of the digits of the encapsulated value.\"\"\"\n        digit_sum = 0\n        current_value = self._value\n        if current_value == 0:\n            return 0\n        while current_value > 0:\n            digit_sum += current_value % 10\n            current_value //= 10\n        return digit_sum\ndef sum_digits(integer_value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the digits of a non-negative integer.\n    This function delegates input validation and the calculation to an internal class.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_negative_int_obj = NonNegativeInteger(integer_value)\n    return non_negative_int_obj.calculate_sum_of_digits()"}
