{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "from typing import List, Any, TypeVar\nComparable = TypeVar('Comparable', bound=Any)\ndef check_min_heap(array: List[Comparable]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array represents a min heap.\n    For every parent node, its value must be less than or equal to the value of its children nodes.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate only through parent nodes, which exist up to index (n // 2) - 1.\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        parent_value = array[i]\n\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        if left_child_idx < n:\n            left_child_value = array[left_child_idx]\n            if parent_value > left_child_value:\n                return False\n\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n        if right_child_idx < n:\n            right_child_value = array[right_child_idx]\n            if parent_value > right_child_value:\n                return False\n\n    return True"}
