{"task_id": "Mbpp/782", "solution": "def odd_length_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all elements across all odd-length subarrays of the input list.\n    Returns an integer representing the total sum.\"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    n = len(arr)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            subarray_length = j - i + 1\n            if subarray_length % 2 == 1:\n                # Sum elements of the current odd-length subarray.\n                for k in range(i, j + 1):\n                    total_sum += arr[k]\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(sorted_list, value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in a sorted list.\n    This function implements binary search to find the index where 'value' should be inserted\n    to maintain sorted order, specifically after any existing equal elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if value < sorted_list[mid]:\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n    return low"}
