{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    \"\"\"\n    def is_natural_number(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is a natural number (i.e., >= 1).\"\"\"\n        return num >= 1\n\n    def is_odd(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is an odd number.\"\"\"\n        return num % 2 != 0\n\n    def validate_range(lower_bound: int, upper_bound: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates the input range against specified business rules.\"\"\"\n        if not is_natural_number(lower_bound) or not is_natural_number(upper_bound):\n            raise ValueError(\"Bounds must be natural numbers (>= 1).\")\n        if lower_bound > upper_bound:\n            raise ValueError(\"Lower bound 'l' must be less than or equal to upper bound 'r'.\")\n\n    validate_range(l, r)\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in range(l, r + 1):\n        if is_odd(num):\n            total_sum += num\n    return total_sum"}
